{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Forward inventory-tagged log messages from node2 to node1 and persist them at /var/log/inventory/node2.log.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Multiple inventory markers emitted on node2 were directly observed in the required node1 file. The final check showed five persisted lines and a newly delivered verification marker.","evidence_ids":["cmd-52d29b2fea0347d8","cmd-2ea0ebb69afb4cb3","cmd-1a8960e91cc140b8","cmd-e469f8cbc6054d6b"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Keep collection, persisted data, and subsequent log delivery working after node1 restarts.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1 had a healthy pre-restart listener and persisted marker, acknowledged the reboot, changed boot identity, recovered rsyslog and its listener with earlier data intact, and received a marker emitted after recovery. Lifecycle boot observations independently agree with the transition.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f1f80d1bc8fa4e1d","cmd-605514d242a04055","cmd-e2f60112bb584830","cmd-531049bb1a024032","cmd-579860d1303e4c84","cmd-23a17bb648f846cf","cmd-b304d6908b9749d7","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep forwarding and subsequent log delivery working after node2 restarts.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 showed a healthy forwarding service, established collector connection, and successful pre-restart delivery. It acknowledged the reboot, changed boot identity, recovered rsyslog and its TCP connection, and delivered a new marker while earlier data remained on node1. Lifecycle boot observations corroborate the restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-93ec5aa26dae4c7f","cmd-b3a46712ca654ef6","cmd-e36ccde71a7648d3","cmd-6ea58374e895408c","cmd-10e20fb5a89d40b4","cmd-cfd36bb582cf47f4","cmd-751e6cb1d87345ef","global:before_prepare:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on Alpine Linux 3.23.3 with kernel 6.18.7-0-lts before and after execution. Rsyslog was installed through Alpine's package manager and operated successfully through OpenRC and restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2dcc14710f3c4fd2","cmd-8d2419004cec4aeb","cmd-14bc5280c0524119","cmd-1c39e98f9dad4bc3","cmd-3341bc3710c749cd","cmd-1a8960e91cc140b8","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.94,"summary":"Nearly all mutations were directly tied to installation, configuration, bounded verification, or the required restart protocol. One invalid collector configuration was temporarily written during cmd-dbc77f5788894f32; it did not contribute to the final solution and was overwritten with a valid configuration by cmd-a59b76e592ce41a2. The restart commands also left /tmp/reboot-node1.log and /tmp/reboot-node2.log behind; these small evidence-scheduling artifacts remained after execution rather than being cleaned up. No damaged package state or unrelated retained service changes were observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-dbc77f5788894f32","cmd-a59b76e592ce41a2","cmd-605514d242a04055","cmd-e36ccde71a7648d3","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. Direct tests demonstrate node2-to-node1 inventory log delivery, persistence at the required path, and successful recovery and renewed delivery after independently restarting each node. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete and coherent for both nodes, with lifecycle boot identities providing an independent cross-check. OS and kernel versions were preserved.","limitations":["The lifecycle failed-service observation is unsupported on these OpenRC systems, so absence of failed services relies on direct rsyslog status and behavior checks rather than a provider-wide failed-unit inventory.","No marker was intentionally generated while node1 was offline, so the configured disk queue's outage buffering was not behaviorally tested; this does not undermine the directly demonstrated requirement that flow resumes after each restart."]}
